===============\r \rbits\(128\) Qin[integer n]\r    assert n >= 0 && n <= 15;\r    return Din[2*n+1]:Din[2*n];)/M(D:20110315114652Z)/IT/Replace/P 516 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">// The 64-bit extension register bank for Advanced SIMD and VFP.&#13; &#13;array bits\(64\) _D[0..31];&#13;&#13;// Clone the 64-bit extension register bank to use as input to instruction pseudocode &#13;// to avoid read-afte\r-write for Advanced SIMD and VFP operations.&#13;&#13;array bits\(64\) _Dclone[0..31];&#13;&#13;&#13;// Din[] - non-assignment form&#13;// ==================&#13; &#13;bits\(64\) Din[integer n]&#13;    assert n &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; n &lt;= 31;&#13;    if n\ &gt;= 16 &amp;&amp; VFPSmallRegisterBank\(\) then UNDEFINED;&#13;    return _Dclone[n];&#13;&#13;&#13;// Qin[] - non-assignment form&#13;// ==================&#13; &#13;bits\(128\) Qin[integer n]&#13;    assert n &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; n &lt;= 15;&#13;    re\turn Din[2*n+1]:Din[2*n];</span></p></body>)/RD[0.474823 0.474823 0.474823 0.474823]/Type/Annot/Popup 522 0 R/AP<</N 16580 0 R>>>>endobj522 0 obj<</Rect[50.5811 172.089 388.981 284.671]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 521 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj523 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110315094202Z)/Rect[460.217 242.449 480.217 260.449]/NM(67f322fe-39a8-4018-a03a-1c9aa637764a)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The replacement pseudocode defines an additional array, _Dclone[], that _D[] can be copied to, to avoiding possible read-after-write errors in instruction processing pseudocode.\r\rIn addition, the function Din[] returns a Doubleword register from the arr\ay _Dclone[], and the function Qin[] returns a Quadword register from the array.)/M(D:20110712122058+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 516 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The replacement pseudocode defines an additional array, _Dclone[], that _D[] can be copied to, to avoiding possible read-after-write errors in instruction processing pseudocode.&#13;&#13;In addition, the function Din[] retur\ns a Doubleword register from the array _Dclone[], and the function Qin[] returns a Quadword register from the array.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 524 0 R/AP<</N 16579 0 R>>>>endobj524 0 obj<</Rect[84.7768 162.872 349.868 437.127]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 523 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj525 0 obj<</Length 2296/Filter/FlateDecode>>stream
