84 469.722 118.98 459.678 411.184 459.678 94.98 456.701 98.1301 456.701 94.98 446.658 98.1301 446.658 118.98 456.701 252.238 456.701 118.98 446.658 252.238 446.658 254.46 455.691 273.9 455.691 254.46 447.058 273.9 447.058 94.98 443.742 98.1301 443.742 94.98 433.698 98.1301 433.698 118.98 443.742 360.558 443.742 118.98 433.698 360.558 433.698]/IRT 1004 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 1003 0 R/AP<</N 16658 0 R>>>>endobj1003 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 362.742 720.0 482.742]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1002 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1004 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20090217105933Z)/Rect[356.503 432.919 365.008 439.849]/NM(a8651af2-a817-460f-8395-462f6f712034)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(\rARMv6T2 adds LDREX and STREX to the Thumb instruction set.\r\rARMv6K has LDREX and STREX in the ARM instruction set only, and adds the following synchronization primitives to the ARM instruction set:\r Ä byte, halfword and doubleword versions of the Loa\d-Exclusive and Store-Exclusive instructions\r Ä a Clear-Exclusive instruction, CLREX.\r\rARMv7 has all of the ARMv6K synchronization primitives in both the ARM and Thumb instruction sets.)/IT/Replace/M(D:20090310123149Z)/P 991 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q1)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p><span style="font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p><p><span style="font-style:normal">ARMv\6T2 adds LDREX and STREX to the Thumb instruction set.&#13;</span></p><p><span style="font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p><p><span style="font-style:normal">ARMv6K has LDREX and STREX in the ARM instruction set only, and adds the following synchronization \primitives to the ARM instruction set:&#13;</span></p><p><span style="font-style:normal"> &#8226; byte, halfword and doubleword versions of the Load-Exclusive and Store-Exclusive instructions&#13;</span></p><p><span style="font-style:normal"> &#8226; a Cl\ear-Exclusive instruction, CLREX.&#13;</span></p><p><span style="font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p><p><span style="font-style:normal">ARMv7 has all of the ARMv6K synchronization primitives in both the ARM and Thumb instruction sets.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.577515 0.577515 0.577515 0.577515]/Type/Annot/Popup 1005 0 R/AP<</N 16659 0 R>>>>endobj1005 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 319.272 720.0 439.272]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1004 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1006 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20090217110048Z)/Rect[496.508 455.997 516.508 473.997]/NM(d33fa8a7-0e80-4aac-99ad-6847524f6804)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 156/Contents(The replacement here only clarifies the wording of the changes in the previous issue of this errata document.)/M(D:20090310123149Z)/Name/Comment/P 991 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q1)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The replacement here only clarifies the wording of the changes in the previous issue of this errata document.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 1007 0 R/AP<</N 16660 0 R>>>>endobj1007 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 342.747 720.0 462.747]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1006 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1008 0 obj<</Length 3384/Filter/FlateDecode>>stream
