?zö\hª√ﬂä®ÛÇTáà7⁄@s%¸˚„6ÔéÕ˜D§ÒØ˘Víı À’¬¢Èâûç®!jëàûí32	_SóKÛ¯I—ÍJ“ó≥!~:ºû¸0,§PdÍ◊;÷®æÔ¶˙J√+H≥°@÷Ø_jåXØ≈f˚¥]ﬁåMÊ¶∏tŒr3Ö«·•ÓØ)gvrÕsÒí(Øìïä7≈Ûx«r-£ùÒ©ßQyº∏¥'‰DHB¥qA'8ù'©ÿ>SsâaVÀîÂ∞L-´≠ˆaQe4,Æ¶ñDqXÚjU;Â\ZEP®K.¨¬©eÀ2WÔXñFœZ÷˙'•&Í$œôï˜áqJ.õÜh EßEû±ôEçõl<xÙü÷‹ü‘Ÿ,Õˇ␀~rÓÃ
endstreamendobj1032 0 obj<</CropBox[0 0 540 648]/Annots[1033 0 R 1034 0 R 1035 0 R 1036 0 R]/Parent 33900 0 R/B[36183 0 R]/Contents 1037 0 R/Rotate 0/MediaBox[0 0 540 648]/Thumb 18403 0 R/Resources<</Font<</T1_0 16547 0 R/T1_1 16548 0 R/T1_2 16545 0 R/T1_3 16554 0 R/T1_4 16551 0 R/T1_5 16556 0 R>>/ProcSet[/PDF/Text]/ExtGState<</GS0 36312 0 R>>>>/Type/Page>>endobj1033 0 obj<</Rect[371.28 528.6 477.66 538.62]/Subtype/Link/Border[0 0 0]/Dest(G7.4959934)/Type/Annot>>endobj1034 0 obj<</Rect[94.98 517.62 303.18 528.6]/Subtype/Link/Border[0 0 0]/Dest(G7.4959934)/Type/Annot>>endobj1035 0 obj<</Rect[128.463 332.522 136.549 339.111]/CreationDate(D:20081106091252Z)/NM(d3f6f723-f9ed-4164-9d32-4e9a5172293a)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(\rFor Shareable regions of memory, in some implementations and for some memory types, the properties of the global monitor can  be met only by functionality outside the processor. Some system implementations might not implement this functionality for all \regions of memory. In particular, this can apply to: \rÄ any type of memory in the system implementation that does not support hardware cache coherency \rÄ Non-cacheable memory, or memory treated as non-cacheable, in an implementation that does support ha\rdware cache coherency. \r\rIn such systems, it is defined by the system:\rÄ whether the global monitor is implemented\rÄ if the global monitor is implemented, which address ranges or memory types it monitors.\r\rThe behavior of Load Exclusive and Store E\xclusive instructions when accessing an address not monitored by the global monitor is UNPREDICTABLE.\r)/M(D:20081124154309Z)/P 1032 0 R/T(ARM_2008_Q4)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">For Shareable regions of memory, in some implementations and for some memory types, the properties of the\ global monitor can  be met only by functionality outside the processor. Some system implementations might not implement this functionality for all regions of memory. In particular, this can apply to: &#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;te\xt-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; any type of memory in the system implementation that does not support hardware cache coherency &#13;&#8226; Non-cacheable memory, or memory treated as non-cacheable, in an implement\ation that does support hardware cache coherency. &#13;&#13;In such systems, it is defined by the system:&#13;&#8226; whether the global monitor is implemented&#13;&#8226; if the global monitor is implemented, which address ranges or memory types it monit\ors.&#13;&#13;The behavior of Load Exclusive and Store Exclusive instructions when accessing an address not monitored by the global monitor is UNPREDICTABLE.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;fo\nt-style:normal">&#13;</span></p></body>)/RD[0.549072 0.549072 0.549072 0.549072]/Type/Annot/Popup 1036 0 R/AP<</N 16675 0 R>>>>endobj1036 0 obj<</Rect[73.3711 214.17 455.624 469.442]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1035 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1037 0 obj<</Length 3510/Filter/FlateDecode>>stream
