26; The effect of a data or unified cache invalidate instruction on a local or global exclusive monitor that is in the Exclusive Access state is UNPREDICTABLE. The operation might clear the monitor, or it might leav\e it in the Exclusive Access state. For address-based invalidation this also applies to the monitors of other processors in the same shareability domain as the processor executing the cache invalidation instruction, as determined by the shareability domai\n of the address being invalidated.&#13;&#13;----- NOTE -----&#13;ARM strongly recommends that implementations ensure that the use of such maintenance instructions by a processor in the Non-secure state cannot cause a denial of service on a processor in t\he Secure state.&#13;-------------------</span></p></body>)/RD[0.587006 0.587006 0.587006 0.587006]/Type/Annot/Popup 1080 0 R/AP<</N 16681 0 R>>>>endobj1080 0 obj<</Rect[137.003 88.8543 526.456 425.289]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1079 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1081 0 obj<</Rect[115.989 176.03 408.025 187.333]/CreationDate(D:20090713122033+01'00')/NM(5bd4a7b9-c4b4-4665-9048-8cc1cc27b672)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/M(D:20090714160030+01'00')/P 1076 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[118.984 186.705 405.03 186.702 118.984 176.661 405.03 176.658]/IRT 1083 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 1082 0 R/AP<</N 16679 0 R>>>>endobj1082 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 66.705 720.0 186.705]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1081 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1083 0 obj<</Rect[398.716 176.106 406.851 182.735]/CreationDate(D:20090713122033+01'00')/NM(31488d47-c848-4989-84d5-40c04cc63263)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(After taking a Data Abort exception, the state of the exclusive monitors is UNKNOWN. Therefore, )/M(D:20090714160030+01'00')/IT/Replace/P 1076 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q2)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">After taking a Data Abort exception, the state of the exclusive monitors is UNKNOWN. Therefore, </span></p></body>)/RD[0.552429 0.552429 0.552429 0.552429]/Type/Annot/Popup 1084 0 R/AP<</N 16678 0 R>>>>endobj1084 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 62.1823 720.0 182.182]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1083 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1085 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20090713122336+01'00')/Rect[488.351 163.92 508.351 181.92]/NM(0787edb7-91c6-4ddc-b4a9-b6a5ea4d40ad)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 156/Contents(This change is a clarification of the intended meaning, not a change to the architecture.)/M(D:20101214104044Z)/Name/Comment/P 1076 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This change is a clarification of the intended meaning, not a change to the architecture.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 1086 0 R/AP<</N 16684 0 R>>>>endobj1086 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 59.1602 720.0 179.16]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1085 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1087 0 obj<</Rect[302.463 370.288 310.585 376.905]/CreationDate(D:20100106105146Z)/NM(42d0d5a5-31e6-467c-bedc-3526794bfbde)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(\rÄ In some implementations, a load to Strongly-ordered or Device memory might clear the exclusive monitor. Therefore, software must not place a load to Strongly-ordered or Device memory between a LDREX and an STREX in a single code sequence.)/M(D:20100225121059Z)/P 1076 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q4)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.1.7" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; In some implementations, a load to Strongly-ordered or Device memory might clear the exclusive mo\nitor. Therefore, software must not place a load to Strongly-ordered or Device memory between a </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">LDREX </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size\:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">and an </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">STREX </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-al\ign:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">in a single code sequence.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.551453 0.551453 0.551453 0.551453]/Type/Annot/Popup 1088 0 R/AP<</N 16677 0 R>>>>endobj1088 0 obj<</Rect[3.58089 461.062 431.653 635.825]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1087 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1089 0 obj<</Rect[116.361 195.05 477.328 206.35]/CreationDate(D:20101214103450Z)/NM(5343b688-d9de-41f0-b6f7-edff3a45db41)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/M(D:20101214103450Z)/P 1076 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[140.64 205.722 153.634 205.722 140.64 195.678 153.634 195.678 177.543 205.722 474.333 205.722 177.543 195.678 474.333 195.678 118.98 204.711 138.422 204.711 118.98 196.078 138.422 196.078 155.88 204.711 175.322 204.711 155.88 196.078 175.322 196.078]/IRT 1091 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 1090 0 R/AP<</N 16682 0 R>>>>endobj1090 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 85.722 720.0 205.722]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1089 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1091 0 obj<</Rect[470.305 194.921 478.481 201.583]/CreationDate(D:20101214103450Z)/NM(3dd52fe7-9f62-48f0-8d88-a5ed111d3449)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(Whether an ARMv7 implementation permits LDREX and STREX operations to a memory region with the Device or Strongly-ordered attribute is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED. Unless the processor documentation explicitly states that the implementation permits these opera\tions, the effect of an LDREX or STREX operation to a memory region with the Device or Strongly-ordered attribute is UNPREDICTABLE.   )/M(D:20101214104242Z)/IT/Replace/P 1076 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">Whether an ARMv7 implementation permits </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">LDREX </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;co\lor:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">and </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">STREX </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-\weight:normal;font-style:normal">operations to a memory region with the Device or Strongly-ordered attribute is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED. Unless the processor documentation explicitly states that the implementation permits these operations, the effect of an\ </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">LDREX </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">or </span><span dir=\"ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">STREX </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">operation to a memory region with the \Device or Strongly-ordered attribute is UNPREDICTABLE.   </span></p></body>)/RD[0.555145 0.555145 0.555145 0.555145]/Type/Annot/Popup 1092 0 R/AP<</N 16683 0 R>>>>endobj1092 0 obj<</Rect[63.0841 56.7096 441.412 201.364]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1091 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1093 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20101214104103Z)/Rect[487.009 187.57 507.009 205.57]/NM(9df5ecad-a6a2-4ee1-b2fe-b1bed9d6a13b)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(This is a change to the architecture. No ARMv7 processors released before January 2011 permit LDREX and STREX operations to memory regions with the Device or Strongly-ordered attribute.)/M(D:20110712122058+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 1076 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This is a change to the architecture. No ARMv7 processors released before January 2011 permit </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">LDREX </span><sp\an dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">and </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">STREX </span><span dir="ltr" styl\e="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">operations to memory regions with the Device or Strongly-ordered attribute.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 1094 0 R/AP<</N 16680 0 R>>>>endobj1094 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 82.2055 720.0 202.205]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1093 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1095 0 obj<</Length 45