iprocessor semantics must be maintained, for example:\r -  respecting dependencies between instructions in a single processor\r -  coherency.\r)/M(D:20081124154309Z)/P 1353 0 R/T(ARM_2008_Q4)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">&lt;new bullet&gt;&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;fo\nt-weight:normal;font-style:normal">For all accesses from a single observer, the requirements of uniprocessor semantics must be maintained, for example:&#13; -  respecting dependencies between instructions in a single processor&#13; -  coherency.&#13;</sp\an></p></body>)/RD[0.549072 0.549072 0.549072 0.549072]/Type/Annot/Popup 1368 0 R/AP<</N 16757 0 R>>>>endobj1368 0 obj<</Rect[216.218 148.874 508.798 287.637]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 1367 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj1369 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20081106084438Z)/Rect[157.505 279.883 165.592 286.472]/NM(c79c96eb-f7ac-4a51-ab22-37158b9b9aa7)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(The size of a memory mapped peripheral, or a block of memory, is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED, but is not smaller than 1KByte.\r<new paragraph>\r)/M(D:20081124154309Z)/P 1353 0 R/T(ARM_2008_Q4)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The size of a memory mapped peripheral, or a block of memory, is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED, but is not smaller than 1KByt