clude a trivial Ja\zelle implementation, an Undefined Instruction might be taken as a result of attempting instruction execution in Jazelle state, see Exception return to an unsupported instruction set state on page B1-40 [PDF page 1190]. If such an Undefined Instruction ex\ception is taken in Jazelle state, exception entry sets the LR to an UNKNOWN value.\r\r)/M(D:20110712122551+01'00')/IT/Replace/P 7687 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q2 and ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">With a non-trivial Jazelle implementation, the architecture does not define any behavior that requires a processor to take an Undefined Instruction exception when it is operating in Jazelle state. However, on some implementa\tions that include a trivial Jazelle implementation, an Undefined Instruction might be taken as a result of attempting instruction execution in Jazelle state, see Exception return to an unsupported instruction set state on page B1-40 [PDF page 1190]. If s\uch an Undefined Instruction exception is taken in Jazelle state, exception entry sets the LR to an UNKNOWN value.&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">&#13;</span></p></bod\y>)/RD[0.48349 0.48349 0.48349 0.48349]/Type/Annot/Popup 7694 0 R/AP<</N 17438 0 R>>>>endobj7694 0 obj<</Rect[28.9529 139.716 360.152 306.625]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 7693 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj7695 0 obj<</Rect[493.547 401.07 513.547 419.07]/CreationDate(D:20110201151914Z)/NM(ca797bc5-347a-4242-8c29-f13536c68497)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(This erratum was updated in the ARM_2010_Q1 errata release, to clarify its intended meaning.)/M(D:20110712122058+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 7687 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This erratum was updated in the ARM_2010_Q1 errata release, to clarify its intended meaning.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 7696 0 R/AP<</N 17437 0 R>>>>endobj7696 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 299.07 720.0 419.07]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 7695 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj7697 0 obj<</Length 3099/Filter/FlateDecode>>stream
