:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The insertion after the modified bit[29] description describes the additional TRCDIS bit, bit[28].&#13;&#13;This optional addition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations. It is not associated with any ARMv7 a\rchitecture extension.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9550 0 R/AP<</N 17697 0 R>>>>endobj9550 0 obj<</Rect[328.314 304.483 508.314 424.265]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 9549 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj9551 0 obj<</Rect[239.91 440.82 248.124 447.513]/CreationDate(D:20110322183449Z)/NM(ec3e6130-7166-434f-9fe7-83e538abfb47)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(TRCDIS, bit[28] \r    Disable CP14 access to trace registers:\r    0	 This bit does not cause any instructions to be undefined.\r    1	 Any MRC or MCR instruction with coproc set to 0b1110 and opc1 set to 0b001 is UNDEFINED.\rOn an implementation that:\r \Ä Does not include a trace macrocell, or does not include a CP14 interface to the trace macrocell registers, this bit is RAZ/WI.\r Ä Includes a CP14 interface to trace macrocell registers, it is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED whether this bit is supported. If it \is not supported it is RAZ/WI.\r\rIf this bit is implemented as an RW bit:\r Ä its reset value is UNKNOWN\r Ä when NSACR.NSTRCDIS is set to 1, it behaves as RAO/WI when accessed from Non-secure state.)/M(D:20110322183458Z)/P 9543 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:bold;font-style:normal">TRCDIS, bit[28] </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;    Disable CP14 access to trace registers:&#13;    0&#9; This bit does not cause any inst\ructions to be undefined.&#13;    1&#9; Any MRC or MCR instruction with coproc set to 0b1110 and opc1 set to 0b001 is UNDEFINED.&#13;On an implementation that:&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:no\rmal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Does not include a trace macrocell, or does not include a CP14 interface to the trace macrocell registers, t\his bit is RAZ/WI.&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:no\rmal">Includes a CP14 interface to trace macrocell registers, it is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED whether this bit is supported. If it is not supported it is RAZ/WI.&#13;&#13;If this bit is implemented as an RW bit:&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.\0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">its reset value is UNKNOWN&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" styl\e="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">when NSACR.NSTRCDIS is set to 1, it behaves a\s RAO/WI when accessed from Non-secure state.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.55777 0.55777 0.55777 0.55777]/Type/Annot/Popup 9552 0 R/AP<</N 17696 0 R>>>>endobj9552 0 obj<</Rect[88.0997 270.622 473.627 398.912]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 9551 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj9553 0 obj<</Rect[133.986 441.03 149.173 452.704]/CreationDate(D:20110322183504Z)/NM(afe77146-dc0b-4c48-85df-d5357cb6b22d)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 4/M(D:20110322183504Z)/P 9543 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[137.08 452.055 146.078 452.055 137.08 441.678 146.078 441.678]/Type/Annot/Popup 9554 0 R/AP<</N 17699 0 R>>>>endobj9554 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 332.055 720.0 452.055]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 9553 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj9555 0 obj<</Length 3299/Filter/FlateDecode>>stream
