al addition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations that include the Security Extensions. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension, other than the Security Extensions.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9598 0 R/AP<</N 17709 0 R>>>>endobj9598 0 obj<</Rect[352.399 210.898 547.453 343.771]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 9597 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj9599 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110318191502Z)/Rect[124.042 247.713 139.231 259.387]/NM(46198d28-aa91-4355-afee-2bc8f2e28d9f)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/M(D:20110318191502Z)/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/P 9588 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[127.137 258.738 136.137 258.738 127.137 248.361 136.137 248.361]/IRT 9601 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 9600 0 R/AP<</N 17707 0 R>>>>endobj9600 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 138.738 720.0 258.738]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 9599 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj9601 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110318191502Z)/Rect[123.032 247.473 131.76 254.584]/NM(7c673a44-6964-4cbb-92d7-c16f43a76480)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(21)/IT/Replace/M(D:20110318191504Z)/P 9588 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">21</span></p></body>)/RD[0.592621 0.592621 0.592621 0.592621]/Type/Annot/Popup 9602 0 R/AP<</N 17710 0 R>>>>endobj9602 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 133.992 720.0 253.992]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 9601 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj9603 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110318191553Z)/Rect[229.769 232.93 237.983 239.623]/NM(6655facd-ba5c-4072-8e39-3312e12da3c3)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(NSTRCDIS, bit[20] \r      Disable Non-secure access to CP14 trace registers:\r        0  This bit has no effect on the ability to write to CPACR.TRCDIS.\r        1  When executing in Non-secure state, CPACR.TRCDIS is RAO/WI.\r\rThe implementation of this \bit depends on the implementation of CPACR.TRCDIS:\r  Ä if CPACR.TRCDIS is RAZ/WI then this bit is RAZ/WI \r  Ä if CPACR.TRCDIS is RW then this bit is RW.\r\rIf this bit is implemented as an RW bit, it resets to 0.)/M(D:20110321183104Z)/P 9588 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:bold;font-style:normal">NSTRCDIS, bit[20]</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#13;      Disable Non-secure access to CP14 trace registers:&#13;        0  This bit has no \effect on the ability to write to CPACR.TRCDIS.&#13;        1  When executing in Non-secure state, CPACR.TRCDIS is RAO/WI.&#13;&#13;The implementation of this bit depends on the implementation of CPACR.TRCDIS:&#13;  </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size\:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">if CPACR.TRCDIS is RAZ/WI then this bit is RAZ/WI &#13;  \</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">if CPACR.TRCDIS is\ RW then this bit is RW.&#13;&#13;If this bit is implemented as an RW bit, it resets to 0.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.557739 0.557739 0.557739 0.557739]/Type/Annot/Popup 9604 0 R/AP<</N 17711 0 R>>>>endobj9604 0 obj<</Rect[85.5644 68.4921 486.146 255.037]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 9603 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj9605 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110318191812Z)/Rect[503.879 218.023 523.879 236.023]/NM(09dff597-3033-4033-9701-986d1551c794)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The insertion after the description of the Reserved field describes the additional NSTRCDIS bit, bit[20].  The reduction in the size of the Reserved field, to become Bits [31:21], is because of this additional bit.\r\rThis optional addition to the NSACR i\s permitted in all ARMv7 implementations that include the Security Extensions. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension other than the Security Extensions.)/M(D:20110712122058+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 9588 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-wei\ght:normal;font-style:normal">The insertion after the description of the Reserved field describes the additional NSTRCDIS bit, bit[20].  The reduction in the size of the Reserved field, to become Bits [31:21], is because of this additional bit.&#13;&#13;T\his optional addition to the NSACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations that include the Security Extensions. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension other than the Security Extensions.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9606 0 R/AP<</N 17705 0 R>>>>endobj9606 0 obj<</Rect[540.0 109.051 720.0 229.051]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 9605 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj9607 0 obj<</Length 3344/Filter/FlateDecode>>stream
