he PC or CPSR do not have that side-effect in Debug state. For example, executing an instruction does not increment the PC. However, the PC and CPSR can be\ updated explicitly in Debug state.)/M(D:20110712122058+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 12062 0 R/T(ghawes)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This statement is not accurate. Processes that, in Non-debug state, have a side-effect of updating the PC or CPSR do not have that side-effect in Debug state. For example, executing an instruction does not increment the PC. \However, the PC and CPSR can be updated explicitly in Debug state.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 12073 0 R/AP<</N 18002 0 R>>>>endobj12073 0 obj<</Rect[225.928 246.689 430.8 407.707]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 12072 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj12074 0 obj<</Length 3371/Filter/FlateDecode>>stream
