esources required by a self-hosted debug tool alive over power-down, does not require any specific support from the Debug architecture.)/M(D:20090710131153+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 12333 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">External debug over power-down, often shortened to debug over power-down, refers only to debug by an external debugger. This requires architectural support to keep the </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align\:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">Debug Communications Channel </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">\(DCC\) and other interfaces to the external debugger \working over a power-down.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;&#13;Self-hosted debug over power-down, meaning keeping the debug resources required by a self-hosted debug t\ool alive over power-down, does not require any specific support from the Debug architecture.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 12338 0 R/AP<</N 18033 0 R>>>>endobj12338 0 obj<</Rect[134.525 428.403 332.853 595.967]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 12337 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj12339 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20090623123023+01'00')/Rect[183.27 461.921 191.619 468.723]/NM(e1819441-11b9-4862-b0a1-54b25a523e5e)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(external )/M(D:20090710121233+01'00')/P 12333 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" st