]/NM(7c6951f1-c5a0-454a-b690-a8a200332379)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 156/Contents(These changes are a clarification of the intended meaning of the description of the TLB matching controls. The ARM_2010_Q3 errata release provides additional clarification of the architectural requirements.\r\rFor bits[3:0], if a bit is unimplemented, it \is RO, and it is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED whether it bit is RAZ or RAO. However, the processor behaves as if the bit is set to 1. This means the corrected comment made in the table about bits[3:2] also applies to bits[1:0].)/M(D:20101021121041+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 13745 0 R/T(ARM_2009_Q4 and ARM_2010_Q3)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">These changes are a clarification of the intended meaning of the description of the TLB matching controls. The ARM_2010_Q3 errata release provides additional clarification of the architectural requirements.&#13;&#13;For bits\[3:0], if a bit is unimplemented, it is RO, and it is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED whether it bit is RAZ or RAO. However, the processor behaves as if the bit is set to 1. This means the corrected comment made in the table about bits[3:2] also applies to bits[1:\0].</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 13764 0 R/AP<</N 18179 0 R>>>>endobj13764 0 obj<</Rect[218.617 91.0764 512.509 247.513]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 13763 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj13765 0 obj<</Rect[131.582 441.056 169.472 452.356]/CreationDate(D:20101020183325+01'00')/NM(3d3deaca-67a7-4f5f-9929-6e7e0e0f3bce)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/M(D:20101020183751+01'00')/P 13745 0 R/T(ARM_2010_Q3)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[134.577 451.728 166.477 451.728 134.577 441.684 166.477 441.684]/IRT 13767 0