er registers\) </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">on page B6-\7 [PDF page 1565], must not be followed by an instruction that accesses banked registers. Software can ensure&#13;this condition is met by inserting a </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-styl\e:normal">NOP </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">instruction after the </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:7.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style\:normal">LDM </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">\(User registers\) instruction.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 15056 0 R/AP<</N 18254 0 R>>>>endobj15056 0 obj<</Rect[40.5177 226.217 332.446 353.199]/Subtype/Popup/Parent 15055 0 R/F 28/Open false/Type/Annot>>endobj15057 0 obj<</Length 1205/Filter/FlateDecode>>stream
