C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/P 7974 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[104.88 102.219 198.131 102.219 104.88 93.586 198.131 93.586 104.88 92.6181 198.131 92.6181 104.88 83.9848 198.131 83.9848 104.88 73.3014 186.489 73.3014 104.88 64.6681 186.489 64.6681]/IRT 7984 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 7983 0 R/AP<</N 17492 0 R>>>>endobj7984 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110315091233Z)/Rect[183.189 64.0662 190.114 69.7085]/NM(32c76086-63f6-4682-8e92-c09df38e18dc)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(// CheckAdvSIMDEnabled\(\)\r// =====================\r\rCheckAdvSIMDEnabled\(\)\r    result = CheckAdvSIMDOrVFPEnabled\(TRUE, TRUE\);\r\r    if result then\r        // Make temporary copy of D registers\r        for i = 0 to 31\r	    _Dclone[i] = _D[i]\r\r\    return result;)/IT/Replace/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/P 7974 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">// CheckAdvSIMDEnabled\(\)&#13;// =====================&#13;&#13;CheckAdvSIMDEnabled\(\)&#13;    result = CheckAdvSIMDOrVFPEnabled\(TRUE, TRUE\);&#13;&#13;    if result then&#13;        // Make temporary copy of D registers&\#13;        for i = 0 to 31&#13;&#9;    _Dclone[i] = _D[i]&#13;&#13;    return result;</span></p></body>)/RD[0.470184 0.470184 0.470184 0.470184]/Type/Annot/Popup 7985 0 R/AP<</N 17495 0 R>>>>endobj7986 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110315091347Z)/Rect[463.066 74.3204 483.066 92.3204]/NM(14ba8f4c-f914-454b-b3b9-e8b381997e6c)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(This change permits instruction pseudocode to use the _Dclone[] array as the input data for the operation, avoiding possible read-after-write errors. See, for example, the corrected instruction pseudocode for VABA on page A8-527 [PDF page 839].)/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 7974 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This change permits instruction pseudocode to use the _Dclone[] array as the input data for the operation, avoiding possible read-after-write errors. See, for example, the corrected instruction pseudocode for VABA on page A8\-527 [PDF page 839].</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 7987 0 R/AP<</N 17493 0 R>>>>endobj8005 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110315091308Z)/Rect[108.006 578.458 284.114 588.171]/NM(8aa0ab49-1d9a-4844-b6e7-afb4e9146fc2)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 4/Contents(See replacement pseudocode on previous page.)/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/P 7989 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[110.58 587.631 281.54 587.631 110.58 578.998 281.54 578.998]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">See replacement pseudocode on previous page.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 8006 0 R/AP<</N 17498 0 R>>>>endobj8075 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110310154711Z)/Rect[258.175 405.989 266.365 412.662]/NM(88d2033b-8bea-4d67-ac5c-2488738a2a96)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(\rFrom the publication of the ARM_2011_Q2 release of this errata PDF, ARM deprecates any use of the ThumbEE instruction set.)/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/P 8060 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;From the publication of the ARM_2011_Q2 release of this errata PDF, ARM deprecates any use of the ThumbEE instruction set.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.556091 0.556091 0.556091 0.556091]/Type/Annot/Popup 8076 0 R/AP<</N 17505 0 R>>>>endobj8077 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110310154722Z)/Rect[491.831 395.087 511.831 413.087]/NM(a8f66a75-c20b-4f32-b9ac-0fd50dab988b)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The insertion after this paragraph deprecates use of the ThumbEE instruction set.)/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 8060 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The insertion after this paragraph deprecates use of the ThumbEE instruction set.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 8078 0 R/AP<</N 17504 0 R>>>>endobj8297 0 obj<</Rect[454.504 93.1443 474.504 111.144]/CreationDate(D:20110203184836Z)/NM(74e3c6ff-cd61-420e-a8e9-bd80ac128585)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The cache maintenance operation is likely to be faster if the following code is used instead of that shown:\r    MRC p15, 1, R0, c0, c0, 1     ; Read CLIDR into R0\r    ANDS R3, R0, #&7000000\r    MOV R3, R3, LSR #23          ; Cache level value \(natural\ly aligned\)\r    BEQ Finished\r    MOV R10, #0\rLoop1 \r    ADD R2, R10, R10, LSR #1   ; Work out 3 x cachelevel\r    MOV R1, R0, LSR R2            ; bottom 3 bits are the Cache type for this level\r    AND R1, R1, #7                   ; get those 3 bits\ alone\r    CMP R1, #2\r    BLT Skip                             ; no cache or only instruction cache at this level\r    MCR p15, 2, R10, c0, c0, 0   ; write CSSELR from R10\r    ISB                                    ; ISB to sync the change to the CCSID\R\r    MRC p15, 1, R1, c0, c0, 0     ; read current CCSIDR to R1\r    AND R2, R1, #&7                 ; extract the line length field\r    ADD R2, R2, #4                   ; add 4 for the line length offset \(log2 16 bytes\)\r    LDR R4, =0x3FF\r    ANDS \R4, R4, R1, LSR #3     ; R4 is the max number on the way size \(right aligned\)\r    CLZ R5, R4                          ; R5 is the bit position of the way size increment\r    MOV R9, R4                        ; R9 working copy of the max way size \(righ\t aligned\)\rLoop2 \r    LDR R7, =0x00007FFF\r    ANDS R7, R7, R1, LSR #13   ; R7 is the max number of the index size \(right aligned\)\rLoop3 \r    ORR R11, R10, R9, LSL R5    ; factor in the way number and cache number into R11\r    ORR R11, R11, R7, LS\L R2    ; factor in the index number\r    MCR p15, 0, R11, c7, c10, 2  ; DCCSW, clean by set/way\r    SUBS R7, R7, #1                  ; decrement the index\r    BGE Loop3\r    SUBS R9, R9, #1                  ; decrement the way number\r    BGE Loop2\r\r\Skip \r    ADD R10, R10, #2                ; increment the cache number\r    CMP R3, R10\r    BGT Loop1\r    DSB\rFinished)/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 8284 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The cache maintenance operation is likely to be faster if the following code is used instead of that shown:&#13;    MRC p15, 1, R0, c0, c0, 1     ; Read CLIDR into R0&#13;    ANDS R3, R0, #&amp;7000000&#13;    MOV R3, R3, LS\R #23          ; Cache level value \(naturally aligned\)&#13;    BEQ Finished&#13;    MOV R10, #0&#13;Loop1 &#13;    ADD R2, R10, R10, LSR #1   ; Work out 3 x cachelevel&#13;    MOV R1, R0, LSR R2            ; bottom 3 bits are the Cache type for this lev\el&#13;    AND R1, R1, #7                   ; get those 3 bits alone&#13;    CMP R1, #2&#13;    BLT Skip                             ; no cache or only instruction cache at this level&#13;    MCR p15, 2, R10, c0, c0, 0   ; write CSSELR from R10&#13;    IS\B                                    ; ISB to sync the change to the CCSIDR&#13;    MRC p15, 1, R1, c0, c0, 0     ; read current CCSIDR to R1&#13;    AND R2, R1, #&amp;7                 ; extract the line length field&#13;    ADD R2, R2, #4               \    ; add 4 for the line length offset \(log2 16 bytes\)&#13;    LDR R4, =0x3FF&#13;    ANDS R4, R4, R1, LSR #3     ; R4 is the max number on the way size \(right aligned\)&#13;    CLZ R5, R4                          ; R5 is the bit position of the way si\ze increment&#13;    MOV R9, R4                        ; R9 working copy of the max way size \(right aligned\)&#13;Loop2 &#13;    LDR R7, =0x00007FFF&#13;    ANDS R7, R7, R1, LSR #13   ; R7 is the max number of the index size \(right aligned\)&#13;Loop3 &\#13;    ORR R11, R10, R9, LSL R5    ; factor in the way number and cache number into R11&#13;    ORR R11, R11, R7, LSL R2    ; factor in the index number&#13;    MCR p15, 0, R11, c7, c10, 2  ; DCCSW, clean by set/way&#13;    SUBS R7, R7, #1               \   ; decrement the index&#13;    BGE Loop3&#13;    SUBS R9, R9, #1                  ; decrement the way number&#13;    BGE Loop2&#13;&#13;Skip &#13;    ADD R10, R10, #2                ; increment the cache number&#13;    CMP R3, R10&#13;    BGT Loop1&#13;\    DSB&#13;Finished</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 8298 0 R/AP<</N 17517 0 R>>>>endobj8305 0 obj<</Rect[472.754 512.316 492.754 530.316]/CreationDate(D:20110712115646+01'00')/NM(84b4dee2-7383-49e5-9059-41f05279ff59)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(See comment on the previous page for an alternative version of this routine, that is likely to be faster. )/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 8300 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">See comment on the previous page for an alternative version of this routine, that is likely to be faster. </span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 8306 0 R/AP<</N 17520 0 R>>>>endobj8537 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110324095329Z)/Rect[115.979 398.021 478.873 479.35]/NM(1a0fd557-61fd-44a0-a43b-912519d0f4b1)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/P 8530 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[118.975 478.722 453.222 478.722 118.975 468.678 453.222 468.678 118.974 467.742 464.455 467.742 118.974 457.698 464.455 457.698 118.974 456.699 475.878 456.699 118.974 446.655 475.878 446.655 118.983 445.719 337.888 445.719 118.983 435.675 337.888 435.675 118.983 430.716 464.671 430.716 118.983 420.672 464.671 420.672 118.983 419.736 474.964 419.736 118.983 409.692 474.964 409.692 118.983 408.693 434.387 408.693 118.983 398.649 434.387 398.649]/Type/Annot/Popup 8538 0 R/AP<</N 17559 0 R>>>>endobj8539 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110324095344Z)/Rect[496.845 464.221 516.845 482.221]/NM(ec2cadd3-f57c-4020-bc78-0667d6293316)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(This bullet is deleted because it was included only as guidance to programmers. However, its intention is not entirely clear, and feedback indicates that it is confusing rather than helpful.\r\rThis deletion does not represent any architectural change, an\d does not affect the validity of the information in the cross-referenced sections.  )/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 8530 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This bullet is deleted because it was included only as guidance to programmers. However, its intention is not entirely clear, and feedback indicates that it is confusing rather than helpful.&#13;&#13;This deletion does not r\epresent any architectural change, and does not affect the validity of the information in the cross-referenced sections.  </span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 8540 0 R/AP<</N 17561 0 R>>>>endobj8673 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110225153734Z)/Rect[473.034 514.274 481.084 520.834]/NM(c316540d-2818-4742-984f-30003ceb3a0f)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(\rTo avoid possible coherency errors caused by mismatched memory attributes, the caches must be maintained after making one of the following changes to the inner cacheability or outer cacheability attributes:\r  Ä Write-back to Write-through \r  Ä Write-b\ack to Non-cacheable\r  Ä Write-through to Non-cacheable\r  Ä Write-through to Write-back.\r\rAfter updating the translation tables, a cache clean and invalidate must be performed to remove the updated locations from the caches.\r\rTo avoid possible coher\ency errors caused by mismatched memory attributes, the following sequence must be followed when changing the shareability attributes of a cacheable memory location:\r 1. Make the memory location Non-cacheable, Outer shareable.\r 2. Clean and invalidate t\he location from them cache.\r 3. Change the shareability attributes to the required new values.\r )/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/P 8662 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;To avoid possible coherency errors caused by mismatched memory attributes, the caches must be maintained after making one of the following changes to the inner cacheability or outer cacheability attributes:&#13;  </span\><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Write-back to Write-thro\ugh &#13;  </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Write-b\ack to Non-cacheable&#13;  </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style\:normal">Write-through to Non-cacheable&#13;  </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weigh\t:normal;font-style:normal">Write-through to Write-back.&#13;&#13;After updating the translation tables, a cache clean and invalidate must be performed to remove the updated locations from the caches.&#13;&#13;To avoid possible coherency errors caused by \mismatched memory attributes, the following sequence must be followed when changing the shareability attributes of a cacheable memory location:&#13; 1. Make the memory location Non-cacheable, Outer shareable.&#13; 2. Clean and invalidate the location from\ them cache.&#13; 3. Change the shareability attributes to the required new values.&#13; </span></p></body>)/RD[0.546631 0.546631 0.546631 0.546631]/Type/Annot/Popup 8674 0 R/AP<</N 17565 0 R>>>>endobj8675 0 obj<</Rect[498.924 429.238 518.924 447.238]/CreationDate(D:20110225155426Z)/NM(e4388a74-d066-4a58-8409-648d9fdce579)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(There is an important addition after this paragraph, that defines the cache maintenance requirements when either:\r Ä changing cacheability attributes\r Ä changing the shareability attributes of a cacheable memory location.)/M(D:20110712123741+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 8662 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">There is an important addition after this paragraph, that defines the cache maintenance requirements when either:&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style\:normal">&#8226; changing cacheability attributes&#13; &#8226; changing the shareability attributes of a cacheable memory location.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 8676 0 R/AP<</N 17564 0 R>>>>endobj8747 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110404154821+01'00')/Rect[113.0 232.886 121.054 239.449]/NM(3d0cb8e8-8dc6-44e8-8d9f-f592f0861010)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents( all of the following apply)/M(D:20110712123741+01'00')/P 8742 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal"> all of the following apply</span></p></body>)/RD[0.546906 0.546906 0.546906 0.546906]/Type/Annot/Popup 8748 0 R/AP<</N 17573 0 R>>>>endobj9034 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110509090629+01'00')/Rect[125.892 219.047 488.791 263.35]/NM(513e7c5e-3cf5-43cb-b6e6-522037766c8a)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/P 9031 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[128.888 262.722 467.74 262.722 128.888 252.678 467.74 252.678 128.892 251.742 485.796 251.742 128.892 241.698 485.796 241.698 128.892 240.699 485.413 240.699 128.892 230.655 485.413 230.655 128.892 229.719 223.141 229.719 128.892 219.675 223.141 219.675]/Type/Annot/Popup 9035 0 R/AP<</N 17609 0 R>>>>endobj9036 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110509090646+01'00')/Rect[498.421 239.984 518.421 257.984]/NM(e343377e-701a-44e4-9b4e-fe4c3d5726f0)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(This statement is deleted because it has no meaning. \rIt is a general requirement that any store operation requires a DSB for it to be visible to translation table walks. Therefore, any store that appears in program order before the TLB maintenance opera\tion requires a DSB to ensure ordering.)/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 9031 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This statement is deleted because it has no meaning. &#13;It is a general requirement that any store operation requires a DSB for it to be visible to translation table walks. Therefore, any store that appears in program orde\r before the TLB maintenance operation requires a DSB to ensure ordering.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9037 0 R/AP<</N 17610 0 R>>>>endobj9085 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20101217165800Z)/Rect[269.816 371.358 292.879 382.159]/NM(4551c1d3-29df-40e1-975b-18c05a8288a4)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit