nsion.)/M(D:20110712123741+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 9529 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The attached file shows the updated CPACR format. Double-click on the pin to see the file. See the insertion after the modified description of bit[29] for more information about the additional bit.&#13;&#13;This optional add\ition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9535 0 R/AP<</N 17693 0 R>>>>endobj9536 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110322183320Z)/Rect[87.4658 332.644 101.466 352.644]/NM(11119f68-c6f7-4db6-b9bc-1bcc25450dbf)/Subtype/FileAttachment/C[0.25 0.333328 1.0]/F 28/Contents(cpacr_format.pdf)/M(D:20110712123741+01'00')/P 9529 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(File Attachment)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p>cpacr_format.pdf</p></body>)/FS 9542 0 R/Type/Annot/AP<</N 17694 0 R>>>>endobj9547 0 obj<</Rect[113.279 441.03 122.969 452.704]/CreationDate(D:20110318190002Z)/NM(3ea6d77c-3315-4432-a2cb-b32f04b64337)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123741+01'00')/P 9543 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[116.374 452.055 119.875 452.055 116.374 441.678 119.875 441.678]/Type/Annot/Popup 9548 0 R/AP<</N 17698 0 R>>>>endobj9549 0 obj<</Rect[507.049 439.857 527.049 457.857]/CreationDate(D:20110318190857Z)/NM(176072f1-949d-4da9-803c-288505b10431)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The insertion after the modified bit[29] description describes the additional TRCDIS bit, bit[28].\r\rThis optional addition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension.)/M(D:20110712123741+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 9543 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The insertion after the modified bit[29] description describes the additional TRCDIS bit, bit[28].&#13;&#13;This optional addition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations. It is not associated with any ARMv7 a\rchitecture extension.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9550 0 R/AP<</N 17697 0 R>>>>endobj9551 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110322183449Z)/Rect[239.91 440.82 248.124 447.513]/NM(ec3e6130-7166-434f-9fe7-83e538abfb47)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(TRCDIS, bit[28] \r    Disable CP14 access to trace registers:\r    0	 This bit does not cause any instructions to be undefined.\r    1	 Any MRC or MCR instruction with coproc set to 0b1110 and opc1 set to 0b001 is UNDEFINED.\rOn an implementation that:\r \Ä Does not include a trace macrocell, or does not include a CP14 interface to the trace macrocell registers, this bit is RAZ/WI.\r Ä Includes a CP14 interface to trace macrocell registers, it is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED whether this bit is supported. If it \is not supported it is RAZ/WI.\r\rIf this bit is implemented as an RW bit:\r Ä its reset value is UNKNOWN\r Ä when NSACR.NSTRCDIS is set to 1, it behaves as RAO/WI when accessed from Non-secure state.)/M(D:20110712123741+01'00')/P 9543 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:bold;font-style:normal">TRCDIS, bit[28] </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;    Disable CP14 access to trace registers:&#13;    0&#9; This bit does not cause any inst\ructions to be undefined.&#13;    1&#9; Any MRC or MCR instruction with coproc set to 0b1110 and opc1 set to 0b001 is UNDEFINED.&#13;On an implementation that:&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:no\rmal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Does not include a trace macrocell, or does not include a CP14 interface to the trace macrocell registers, t\his bit is RAZ/WI.&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:no\rmal">Includes a CP14 interface to trace macrocell registers, it is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED whether this bit is supported. If it is not supported it is RAZ/WI.&#13;&#13;If this bit is implemented as an RW bit:&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.\0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">its reset value is UNKNOWN&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" styl\e="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">when NSACR.NSTRCDIS is set to 1, it behaves a\s RAO/WI when accessed from Non-secure state.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.55777 0.55777 0.55777 0.55777]/Type/Annot/Popup 9552 0 R/AP<</N 17696 0 R>>>>endobj9553 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110322183504Z)/Rect[133.986 441.03 149.173 452.704]/NM(afe77146-dc0b-4c48-85df-d5357cb6b22d)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123741+01'00')/P 9543 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[137.08 452.055 146.078 452.055 137.08 441.678 146.078 441.678]/Type/Annot/Popup 9554 0 R/AP<</N 17699 0 R>>>>endobj34128 0 obj<</Subtype/XML/Length 3920/Type/Metadata>>stream
