ut the additional bit.&#13;&#13;This opt\ional addition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations that include the Security Extensions. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension, other than the Security Extensions.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9598 0 R/AP<</N 17709 0 R>>>>endobj9599 0 obj<</Rect[124.042 247.713 139.231 259.387]/CreationDate(D:20110318191502Z)/NM(46198d28-aa91-4355-afee-2bc8f2e28d9f)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 9588 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[127.137 258.738 136.137 258.738 127.137 248.361 136.137 248.361]/IRT 9601 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 9600 0 R/AP<</N 17707 0 R>>>>endobj9601 0 obj<</Rect[123.032 247.473 131.76 254.584]/CreationDate(D:20110318191502Z)/NM(7c673a44-6964-4cbb-92d7-c16f43a76480)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(21)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/IT/Replace/P 9588 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">21</span></p></body>)/RD[0.592621 0.592621 0.592621 0.592621]/Type/Annot/Popup 9602 0 R/AP<</N 17710 0 R>>>>endobj9603 0 obj<</Rect[229.769 232.93 237.983 239.623]/CreationDate(D:20110318191553Z)/NM(6655facd-ba5c-4072-8e39-3312e12da3c3)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(NSTRCDIS, bit[20] \r      Disable Non-secure access to CP14 trace registers:\r        0  This bit has no effect on the ability to write to CPACR.TRCDIS.\r        1  When executing in Non-secure state, CPACR.TRCDIS is RAO/WI.\r\rThe implementation of this \bit depends on the implementation of CPACR.TRCDIS:\r  Ä if CPACR.TRCDIS is RAZ/WI then this bit is RAZ/WI \r  Ä if CPACR.TRCDIS is RW then this bit is RW.\r\rIf this bit is implemented as an RW bit, it resets to 0.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 9588 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:bold;font-style:normal">NSTRCDIS, bit[20]</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#13;      Disable Non-secure access to CP14 trace registers:&#13;        0  This bit has no \effect on the ability to write to CPACR.TRCDIS.&#13;        1  When executing in Non-secure state, CPACR.TRCDIS is RAO/WI.&#13;&#13;The implementation of this bit depends on the implementation of CPACR.TRCDIS:&#13;  </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size\:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">if CPACR.TRCDIS is RAZ/WI then this bit is RAZ/WI &#13;  \</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">if CPACR.TRCDIS is\ RW then this bit is RW.&#13;&#13;If this bit is implemented as an RW bit, it resets to 0.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.557739 0.557739 0.557739 0.557739]/Type/Annot/Popup 9604 0 R/AP<</N 17711 0 R>>>>endobj9605 0 obj<</Rect[503.879 218.023 523.879 236.023]/CreationDate(D:20110318191812Z)/NM(09dff597-3033-4033-9701-986d1551c794)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The insertion after the description of the Reserved field describes the additional NSTRCDIS bit, bit[20].  The reduction in the size of the Reserved field, to become Bits [31:21], is because of this additional bit.\r\rThis optional addition to the NSACR i\s permitted in all ARMv7 implementations that include the Security Extensions. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension other than the Security Extensions.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 9588 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-wei\ght:normal;font-style:normal">The insertion after the description of the Reserved field describes the additional NSTRCDIS bit, bit[20].  The reduction in the size of the Reserved field, to become Bits [31:21], is because of this additional bit.&#13;&#13;T\his optional addition to the NSACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations that include the Security Extensions. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension other than the Security Extensions.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9606 0 R/AP<</N 17705 0 R>>>>endobj9616 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110321183115Z)/Rect[501.344 572.957 521.344 590.957]/NM(33da01b3-2039-4a65-9bbd-85ef8a9af9eb)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The implementation of the NSASEDIS bit must correspond to the implementation of CPACR.ASED:\r Ä if CPACR.ASED is not RW then NSASEDIS is RAZ/WI\r Ä if CPACR.ASED is RW then NSASEDIS is RW.\r)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 9613 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The implementation of the NSASEDIS bit must correspond to the implementation of CPACR.ASED:&#13; &#8226; if CPACR.ASED is not RW then NSASEDIS is RAZ/WI&#13; &#8226; if CPACR.ASED is RW then NSASEDIS is RW.&#13;</span></p></\body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9617 0 R/AP<</N 17713 0 R>>>>endobj9618 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110321183115Z)/Rect[503.07 408.61 523.07 426.61]/NM(eab44de9-88f8-4346-91a7-153ded6ea166)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The implementation of the NSD32DIS bit must correspond to the implementation of CPACR.D32DIS:\r Ä if CPACR.D32DIS is not RW then NSD32DIS is RAZ/WI\r Ä if CPACR.D32DIS is RW then NSD32DIS is RW.\r\r)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 9613 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The implementation of the NSD32DIS bit must correspond to the implementation of CPACR.D32DIS:&#13; &#8226; if CPACR.D32DIS is not RW then NSD32DIS is RAZ/WI&#13; &#8226; if CPACR.D32DIS is RW then NSD32DIS is RW.&#13;&#13;</\span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 9619 0 R/AP<</N 17712 0 R>>>>endobj9753 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20101217164003Z)/Rect[261.894 515.01 284.957 525.811]/NM(bece8a79-6053-4e11-9806-90837cd8e8dc)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/P 9743 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[264.757 525.211 282.094 525.211 264.757 515.61 282.094 515.61]/IRT 9755 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 9754 0 R/AP<</N 17717 0 R>>>>endobj9755 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20101217164003Z)/Rect[278.349 514.751 286.354 521.273]/NM(8d0ecdaa-b0ad-4dc8-bf7a-58654cf321ba)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(UNPREDICTABLE)/IT/Replace/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 9743 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0