9-4372-bc7b-ebe3648f3512)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(This correction to the pseudocode identifies some additional UNPREDICTABLE cases that are shown correctly in Table C10-11 on page C10-56 [PDF page 1824].)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 11919 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This correction to the pseudocode identifies some additional UNPREDICTABLE cases that are shown correctly in Table C10-11 on page C10-56 [PDF page 1824].</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 11926 0 R/AP<</N 17989 0 R>>>>endobj12070 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110330180740+01'00')/Rect[149.888 281.912 475.495 293.212]/NM(b18ac44c-c486-405c-b3ef-7c7622b76590)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 12062 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[152.883 292.584 472.5 292.584 152.883 282.54 472.5 282.54]/Type/Annot/Popup 12071 0 R/AP<</N 18003 0 R>>>>endobj12072 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110330180755+01'00')/Rect[496.916 280.934 516.916 298.934]/NM(1a1e052a-3eda-4f6e-8ea7-b9dda3b5f6f9)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(This statement is not accurate. Processes that, in Non-debug state, have a side-effect of updating the PC or CPSR do not have that side-effect in Debug state. For example, executing an instruction does not increment the PC. However, the PC and CPSR can be\ updated explicitly in Debug state.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 12062 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">This statement is not accurate. Processes that, in Non-debug state, have a side-effect of updating the PC or CPSR do not have that side-effect in Debug state. For example, executing an instruction does not increment the PC. \However, the PC and CPSR can be updated explicitly in Debug state.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 12073 0 R/AP<</N 18002 0 R>>>>endobj12546 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20101118165056Z)/Rect[482.477 155.864 502.477 173.864]/NM(c11170df-d709-499a-a82b-a11e583f6471)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(To clarify the intended meaning of the replacement text:\rThe events listed can be described as context synchronization operations.\r Ä Without a context synchronization operation, the  change becomes visible at some point after the instruction that chang\ed the memory-mapped debug registers. \r Ä However, until a context synchronization operation has occurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.\r)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 12540 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">To clarify the intended meaning of the replacement text:&#13;The events listed can be described as </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">context syn\chronization operations</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#\13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Without a </sp\an><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation, the </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style\:normal"> change becomes visible at some point after the instruction that changed the memory-mapped debug registers. &#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; However, u\ntil a </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-\style:normal"> has occurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 12547 0 R/AP<</N 18060 0 R>>>>endobj12548 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20101118165056Z)/Rect[489.894 396.39 509.894 414.39]/NM(26aebe73-1b4a-4728-b5c6-1c4631ef136b)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(To clarify the intended meaning of this text:\rThe events listed can be described as context synchronization operations.\r Ä Without a context synchronization operation, the  change becomes visible at some point after the instruction that changed the CP14\ debug registers. \r Ä However, until a context synchronization operation has occurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.\r)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 12540 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">To clarify the intended meaning of this text:&#13;The events listed can be described as </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">context synchronizatio\n operations</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span><\span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Without a </span><span di\r="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation, the </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> c\hange becomes visible at some point after the instruction that changed the CP14 debug registers. &#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; However, until a </span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> has o\ccurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 12549 0 R/AP<</N 18059 0 R>>>>endobj14265 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110404155936