bj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal"> </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> However, user feedback indicates a number of cases where these instructions are useful. Therefore, ARM no lo\nger deprecates these instruction uses.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.547302 0.547302 0.547302 0.547302]/Type/Annot/Popup 14437 0 R/AP<</N 18232 0 R>>>>endobj14438 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110616154221+01'00')/Rect[498.877 442.921 518.877 460.921]/NM(7a93a385-c78e-4837-8d7a-f2736d7a508c)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The insertion at the end of this line removes the earlier deprecation.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 14403 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The insertion at the end of this line removes the earlier deprecation.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 14439 0 R/AP<</N 18231 0 R>>>>endobj14440 0 obj<</Rect[411.331 454.067 471.253 465.367]/CreationDate(D:20110620095212+01'00')/NM(8e33d0f4-3ee3-4963-8703-cc55999b7299)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 4/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 14403 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[414.326 464.739 468.258 464.739 414.326 454.695 468.258 454.695]/Type/Annot/Popup 14441 0 R/AP<</N 18228 0 R>>>>endobj16488 0 obj<</Rect[92.0149 268.055 478.578 290.335]/CreationDate(D:20110616164806+01'00')/NM(aec35846-0d5f-4d85-8884-3b3a02e6ea03)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 16486 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[95.01 289.707 475.583 289.707 95.01 279.663 475.583 279.663 95.01 278.727 383.597 278.727 95.01 268.683 383.597 268.683]/IRT 16490 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 16489 0 R/AP<</N 18267 0 R>>>>endobj16490 0 obj<</Rect[379.415 267.988 387.476 274.555]/CreationDate(D:20110616164806+01'00')/NM(c2887c06-fb5d-48df-a925-4ed79a5520de)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 4/Contents(In the ARM architecture, domain is used in the following contexts.\rShareability domain \rDefines a set of observers for which the shareability attributes make the data or unified caches transparent for data accesses.\rPower domain \rDefines a block of lo\gic with a single, common, power supply.\rMemory regions domain \rDefines a collection of Sections, Large pages and Small pages of memory, that can have their access permissions switched rapidly by writing to the Domain Access Control Register \(DACR\). A\RM deprecates any use of memory regions domains.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/IT/Replace/P 16486 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Replacement Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">In the ARM architecture, </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">domain</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;f\ont-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> is used in the following contexts.&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal">Shareability domain</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt\;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#13;Defines a set of observers for which the shareability attributes make the data or unified caches transparent for data accesses.&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;t\ext-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal">Power domain</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#13;Defines a block of logic with a single, common, power sup\ply.&#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal">Memory regions domain &#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style\:normal">Defines a collection of Sections, Large pages and Small pages of memory, that can have their access permissions switched rapidly by writing to the </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;fon\t-style:italic">Domain Access Control Register</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> \(DACR\). ARM deprecates any use of memory regions domains.</span></p></body>)/RD[0.547302 0.547302 0.547302 0.547302]/Type/Annot/Popup 16491 0 R/AP<</N 18266 0 R>>>>endobj16492 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110616164933+01'00')/Rect[496.887 269.11 516.887 287.11]/NM(341fc1ef-7324-4932-8650-61898ecc7a7b)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 28/Contents(The current definition includes only one of the three contexts in which Domain is used.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 16486 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The current definition includes only one of the three contexts in which Domain is used.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 16493 0 R/AP<</N 18268 0 R>>>>endobj34128 0 obj<</Subtype/XML/Length 3920/Type/Metadata>>stream
