ing the width of any instruction fetch when CPSR.{J, T} correspond to an unimplemented instruction set state.)/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 7734 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">See inserted statement, intended to follow the bulleted list, regarding the width of any instruction fetch when CPSR.{J, T} correspond to an unimplemented instruction set state.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 7749 0 R/AP<</N 17452 0 R>>>>endobj7750 0 obj<</Rect[90.8184 105.915 98.8728 112.478]/CreationDate(D:20110401092359+01'00')/NM(f421e802-05dc-499b-bd4a-0f53ed1f91f3)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(If an exception return writes CPSR.{J, T} values that correspond to an unimplemented instruction set, the width of the instruction fetch is an IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED value that is 1, 2 or 4 bytes.\r\r)/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/P 7734 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">If an exception return writes CPSR.{J, T} values that correspond to an unimplemented instruction set, the width of the instruction fetch is an IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED value that is 1, 2 or 4 bytes.&#13;&#13;</span></p></body>\)/RD[0.546906 0.546906 0.546906 0.546906]/Type/Annot/Popup 7751 0 R/AP<</N 17446 0 R>>>>endobj7799 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110321144641Z)/Rect[397.726 117.941 405.966 129.241]/NM(b3486fe8-64c8-4dc9-a016-2db12de76d27)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/M(D:20110712123706+01'00')/IT/Strike