0 obj<</Rect[477.344 471.527 497.344 489.527]/CreationDate(D:20101118164917Z)/NM(de973441-7797-4d6e-81d2-9178a8920f32)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 156/Contents(To clarify the intended meaning of this statement:\rThe events listed can be described as context synchronization operations.\r Ä Without a context synchronization operation, the  change becomes visible at some point after the instruction that changed the\ CP15 registers. \r Ä However, until a context synchronization operation has occurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.\r)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 10470 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">To clarify the intended meaning of this statement:&#13;The events listed can be described as </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">context synchroni\zation operations</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</s\pan><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Without a </span><sp\an dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation, the </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l"> change becomes visible at some point after the instruction that changed the CP15 registers. &#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; However, until a </span><span d\ir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> has oc\curred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 10473 0 R/AP<</N 17807 0 R>>>>endobj10474 0 obj<</Rect[141.584 248.254 148.785 254.12]/CreationDate(D:20101214140441Z)/NM(5b6bafe0-c4b9-4621-8a6f-ad1f466cc2ad)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(0, )/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 10470 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">0, </span></p></body>)/RD[0.488892 0.488892 0.488892 0.488892]/Type/Annot/Popup 10475 0 R/AP<</N 17808 0 R>>>>endobj10707 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110318190953Z)/Rect[99.7125 304.679 501.14 388.567]/NM(357a9004-c479-4e13-bfee-c9e4dcf41df0)/Subtype/Line/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 132/L[105.213 310.179 495.64 383.067]/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 10704 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Line)/Type/Annot/Popup 10708 0 R/AP<</N 17854 0 R>>>>endobj10709 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110318191028Z)/Rect[501.344 346.053 521.344 364.053]/NM(34b55ac9-220c-4acc-a6e6-05b862940f7a)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 156/Contents(The attached file shows the updated CPACR format. Double-click on the pin to see the file. See the insertion after the modified description of bit[29] for more information about the additional bit.\r\rThis optional addition to the CPACR is permitted in al\l ARMv7 implementations. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 10704 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The attached file shows the updated CPACR format. Double-click on the pin to see the file. See the insertion after the modified description of bit[29] for more information about the additional bit.&#13;&#13;This optional add\ition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 10710 0 R/AP<</N 17853 0 R>>>>endobj10711 0 obj<</Rect[98.2406 343.419 112.241 363.419]/CreationDate(D:20110322183739Z)/NM(619423cf-5f20-4758-a9db-142a3f8faefb)/Subtype/FileAttachment/C[0.25 0.333328 1.0]/F 156/Contents(cpacr_format.pdf)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 10704 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(File Attachment)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p>cpacr_format.pdf</p></body>)/FS 10717 0 R/Type/Annot/AP<</N 17694 0 R>>>>endobj10723 0 obj<</CreationDate(D:20110318191056Z)/Rect[510.217 391.053 530.217 409.053]/NM(58145dd4-8dfd-4487-a309-de3d268da347)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 156/Contents(The insertion after the modified bit[29] description describes the additional TRCDIS bit, bit[28].\r\rThis optional addition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations. It is not associated with any ARMv7 architecture extension.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 10718 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">The insertion after the modified bit[29] description describes the additional TRCDIS bit, bit[28].&#13;&#13;This optional addition to the CPACR is permitted in all ARMv7 implementations. It is not associated with any ARMv7 a\rchitecture extension.</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 10724 0 R/AP<</N 17855 0 R>>>>endobj10725 0 obj<</Rect[103.397 396.03 113.087 407.704]/CreationDate(D:20110322183756Z)/NM(c786e81d-fd9c-428f-a655-3be28b329a6d)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 132/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 10718 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[106.491 407.055 109.992 407.055 106.491 396.678 109.992 396.678]/Type/Annot/Popup 10726 0 R/AP<</N 17858 0 R>>>>endobj10727 0 obj<</Rect[121.057 396.03 139.243 407.704]/CreationDate(D:20110322183803Z)/NM(355e0ba2-71ee-41ec-95e4-bf2269eb889a)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[1.0 0.0 0.0]/F 132/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 10718 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[124.152 407.055 136.149 407.055 124.152 396.678 136.149 396.678]/Type/Annot/Popup 10728 0 R/AP<</N 17856 0 R>>>>endobj10729 0 obj<</Rect[229.769 395.819 237.983 402.513]/CreationDate(D:20110322183825Z)/NM(106b0b3f-7d08-4377-8317-b52a2aeb0f07)/Subtype/Caret/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/Contents(TRCDIS, bit[28] \r    Disable CP14 access to trace registers:\r    0	 This bit does not cause any instructions to be undefined.\r    1	 Any MRC or MCR instruction with coproc set to 0b1110 and opc1 set to 0b001 is UNDEFINED.\r\rOn an implementation that:\r\ Ä Does not include a trace macrocell, or does not include a CP14 interface to the trace macrocell registers, this bit is RAZ/WI.\r Ä Includes a CP14 interface to trace macrocell registers, it is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED whether this bit is supported. If it\ is not supported it is RAZ/WI.\r\rIf this bit is implemented as an RW bit its reset value is UNKNOWN.)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 10718 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Inserted Text)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:bold;font-style:normal">TRCDIS, bit[28] </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;    Disable CP14 access to trace registers:&#13;    0&#9; This bit does not cause any inst\ructions to be undefined.&#13;    1&#9; Any MRC or MCR instruction with coproc set to 0b1110 and opc1 set to 0b001 is UNDEFINED.&#13;&#13;On an implementation that:&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weig\ht:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Does not include a trace macrocell, or does not include a CP14 interface to the trace macrocell registe\rs, this bit is RAZ/WI.&#13; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-sty\le:normal">Includes a CP14 interface to trace macrocell registers, it is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED whether this bit is supported. If it is not supported it is RAZ/WI.&#13;&#13;If this bit is implemented as an RW bit its reset value is UNKNOWN.</span></p></bo\dy>)/RD[0.55777 0.55777 0.55777 0.55777]/Type/Annot/Popup 10730 0 R/AP<</N 17857 0 R>>>>endobj10874 0 obj<</Rect[261.894 514.687 284.957 525.488]/CreationDate(D:20101217164138