0 R/AP<</N 18002 0 R>>>>endobj12546 0 obj<</Rect[482.477 155.864 502.477 173.864]/CreationDate(D:20101118165056Z)/NM(c11170df-d709-499a-a82b-a11e583f6471)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 156/Contents(To clarify the intended meaning of the replacement text:\rThe events listed can be described as context synchronization operations.\r Ä Without a context synchronization operation, the  change becomes visible at some point after the instruction that chang\ed the memory-mapped debug registers. \r Ä However, until a context synchronization operation has occurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.\r)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 12540 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.5" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">To clarify the intended meaning of the replacement text:&#13;The events listed can be described as </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">context syn\chronization operations</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#\13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Without a </sp\an><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation, the </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style\:normal"> change becomes visible at some point after the instruction that changed the memory-mapped debug registers. &#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; However, u\ntil a </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-\style:normal"> has occurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 12547 0 R/AP<</N 18060 0 R>>>>endobj12548 0 obj<</Rect[489.894 396.39 509.894 414.39]/CreationDate(D:20101118165056Z)/NM(26aebe73-1b4a-4728-b5c6-1c4631ef136b)/Subtype/Text/CA 0.505005/C[1.0 1.0 0.0]/F 156/Contents(To clarify the intended meaning of this text:\rThe events listed can be described as context synchronization operations.\r Ä Without a context synchronization operation, the  change becomes visible at some point after the instruction that changed the CP14\ debug registers. \r Ä However, until a context synchronization operation has occurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.\r)/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/Name/Comment/P 12540 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Sticky Note)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:8.2.6" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-we\ight:normal;font-style:normal">To clarify the intended meaning of this text:&#13;The events listed can be described as </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">context synchronizatio\n operations</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span><\span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Without a </span><span di\r="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation, the </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> c\hange becomes visible at some point after the instruction that changed the CP14 debug registers. &#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> &#8226; However, until a </span><span \dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">context synchronization operation</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"> has o\ccurred, the architecture does not guarantee that the change is visible.</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p></body>)/Type/Annot/Popup 12549 0 R/AP<</N 18059 0 R>>>>endobj14265 0 obj<</Rect[193.533 140.024 220.568 151.324]/CreationDate(D:20110404155936+01'00')/NM(1a44437f-d02a-4b85-b8f0-f3f933007bfa)/Subtype/StrikeOut/C[0.0 0.0 1.0]/F 132/IT/StrikeOutTextEdit/M(D:20110712123917+01'00')/P 14252 0 R/T(ARM_2011_Q2)/Subj(Cross-Out)/QuadPoints[196.528 150.696 217.573 150.696 196.528 140.652 217.573 140.652]/IRT 14267 0 R/RT/Group/Type/Annot/Popup 14266 0 R/AP<</N 18209 0 R>>>>endobj14267 0 obj<</Rect[